cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Domain-Adaptive Calibrated Routing (DACR) for LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dogani
    given-names: Javad
    affiliation: IMDEA Networks Institute
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JavadDogani/domain-adaptive-calibrated-routing"
abstract: >-
  Per-prompt LLM routing that keeps answer quality high while average cost (and optionally
  latency) stays within a budget: calibrated per-domain quality predictors, leakage-free cost and
  latency estimates, online Lagrangian budget pacing with delayed feedback, and an optional residual
  contextual bandit, with an evaluation harness on RouterBench.
keywords:
  - llm-routing
  - calibration
  - domain-adaptation
  - contextual-bandits
  - routerbench
